# Minimum total statement coverage, in percent, that `scripts/coverage.sh`
# enforces. This is the single source of truth: `task coverage` and CI both read
# it from here, so raising the ratchet is a one-line change in one file.
#
# awesome-go's quality standard asks for >=80% per non-data package. The repo is
# not there yet, so this starts at the measured baseline and only moves up. See
# docs/awesome-go-submission.md and CONTRIBUTING.md.
#
# 70.9 is 6811 covered of 9602 statements, as computed by scripts/coverage.sh.
# `go tool cover -func` reports 71.0% for the same profile: it attributes blocks
# to declared functions and drops what it cannot place, so its denominator is
# slightly smaller. The 0.1pp gap is methodology, not a coverage change. The
# ratchet has to be enforced against the number this script actually produces, and
# the per-package figures it prints match `go test`'s own per-package output.
70.9
